{"tool_name":"allpaths-lg","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"allpaths-lg","home":"https://www.broadinstitute.org/computational-rd/computational-research-and-development","license":"MIT","summary":"Short read assembler that works on both small and large (mammalian size) genomes.","addition_date":"2017-08-20T15:00:39Z","last_update_date":"2021-05-27T09:42:43Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"collections":["Animal and Crop Genomics"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:allpaths-lg","credit":[{"email":"jaffe@broadinstitute.org","name":"David B. Jaffe","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://groups.google.com/a/broadinstitute.org/forum/?hl=en&fromgroups#!forum/discovar-user-forum"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://www.broadinstitute.org/computational-rd/computational-research-and-development"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"ftp://ftp.broadinstitute.org/pub/crd/ALLPATHS/Release-LG/AllPaths-LG_Manual.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["animalandcropgenomics"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genetic variation analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3197"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"}]}],"name":"Allpaths-LG","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"admin","publication":[{"doi":"10.1073/pnas.1017351108","metadata":{"abstract":"Massively parallel DNA sequencing technologies are revolutionizing genomics by making it possible to generate billions of relatively short (\u223c100-base) sequence reads at very low cost. Whereas such data can be readily used for a wide range of biomedical applications, it has proven difficult to use them to generate high-quality de novo genome assemblies of large, repeat-rich vertebrate genomes. To date, the genome assemblies generated from such data have fallen far short of those obtained with the older (but much more expensive) capillary-based sequencing approach. Here, we report the development of an algorithm for genome assembly, ALLPATHS-LG, and its application to massively parallel DNA sequence data from the human and mouse genomes, generated on the Illumina platform. The resulting draft genome assemblies have good accuracy, short-range contiguity, long-range connectivity, and coverage of the genome. In particular, the base accuracy is high (\u226599.95%) and the scaffold sizes (N50 size = 11.5 Mb for human and 7.2 Mb for mouse) approach those obtained with capillary-based sequencing. The combination of improved sequencing technology and improved computational methods should now make it possible to increase dramatically the de novo sequencing of large genomes. The ALLPATHS-LG program is available at http://www.broadinstitute.org/science/programs/genome-biology/crd.","authors":[{"name":"Aird D."},{"name":"Berlin A.M."},{"name":"Burton J.N."},{"name":"Costello M."},{"name":"Daza R."},{"name":"Gnerre S."},{"name":"Gnirke A."},{"name":"Hall G."},{"name":"Jaffe D.B."},{"name":"Lander E.S."},{"name":"MacCallum I."},{"name":"Nicol R."},{"name":"Nusbaum C."},{"name":"Przybylski D."},{"name":"Ribeiro F.J."},{"name":"Sharpe T."},{"name":"Shea T.P."},{"name":"Sykes S."},{"name":"Walker B.J."},{"name":"Williams L."}],"citationCount":1088,"date":"2011-01-25T00:00:00Z","journal":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","title":"High-quality draft assemblies of mammalian genomes from massively parallel sequence data"},"pmcid":"PMC3029755","pmid":"21187386","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Genetic variation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0199"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0196"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Allpaths-LG","home":"https://bio.tools/allpaths-lg","license":"MIT","summary":"Short read assembler that works on both small and large (mammalian size) genomes.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor